{
  // Shared declaration-emit config for every workspace package's
  // `tsconfig.build.json`, sitting beside `tsconfig.base.json` (which owns the
  // type-checking semantics). A package's `build` script runs Vite library mode
  // for the JS bundle and then `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json` for the .d.ts files,
  // because Vite's lib mode emits no declarations — so all seven packages had
  // byte-identical settings here before this file existed.
  //
  // `${configDir}` is what makes this hoistable at all, and it is not optional.
  // TypeScript normally resolves a relative path against the directory of the
  // file the path is WRITTEN in, so a plain `"outDir": "dist"` here would mean
  // `<repo>/dist` and every package would emit its declarations on top of each
  // other in one shared directory. Measured, not assumed: a base carrying a
  // plain `outDir` built packages/query into `packages/dist` and produced no
  // `packages/query/dist` at all. `${configDir}` instead resolves against the
  // directory of the config doing the extending (TypeScript 5.5+), which is the
  // per-package `tsconfig.build.json` — so each package emits into its own
  // `dist/`, and this file can be moved without rewriting the paths.
  //
  // `rootDir` is set rather than inferred so `dist/` mirrors `src/`; TS7 fails
  // with error TS5011 without it.
  //
  // What stays per-package is `include`: the hand-listed public entry points.
  // That is load-bearing. tsc transitively pulls in every real src file an entry
  // imports, so listing the entries is what keeps *.test.ts, scripts and root
  // *.config.ts out of the declaration program and stops a stray .d.ts leaking
  // into dist/. An entry nothing else imports — the SDK's
  // `server/passthrough.ts`, deliberately unreferenced so a passthrough-only app
  // never reaches the BFF handler graph — must be listed explicitly or it emits
  // no .d.ts at all.
  //
  // NOTE for anyone editing `exclude` below: a package that declares its own
  // `exclude` REPLACES this list rather than merging with it. No package does
  // today; if one needs to add an entry, it has to restate these three.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "declaration": true,
    "emitDeclarationOnly": true,
    "rootDir": "${configDir}/src",
    "outDir": "${configDir}/dist"
  },
  "exclude": [
    "${configDir}/**/*.test.ts",
    "${configDir}/**/*.test.tsx",
    "${configDir}/**/*.config.ts"
  ]
}
